Although we do of course admit that physical matter exists, this matter is not the one prime creator of sentient beings in the way that mind is. Therefore all these scriptural references are denying that the opposite of the mind, something other than the mind, could be the creator. They are not though saying that there are no outside physical objects at all. The Asian Classics Institute Reading Two: How Emptiness Allows Karma to Work, According to the Middle-Way School\", \"wylie_method\": \"glyph-decode\", \"decode_score\": 1.0}"
